            <ArticleTitle>Enantio- and Diastereoselective Dehydrative &quot;One-Step&quot; Construction of Spirocarbocycles via a Ru/H+ -Catalyzed Tsuji-Trost Approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>633-637</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/asia.201700013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chiral spirocarbocyclic skeletons are ubiquitous in natural products. An intramolecular Tsuji-Trost (T-T) α-allylation of simple cyclic ketones is a reasonable approach to construct chiral spriocarbocyclic motifs; however, it has been a challenging approach despite many excellent intermolecular examples. For the first time, this has been achieved by a Ru/H+ combined catalyst that dehydratively cyclizes racemic allylic alcohols comprising a simple ketone via simultaneous activation of the C=O and OH groups. This chiral technology facilitates the construction of various spirocarbocycles containing two contiguous spiro all-carbon quaternary and tertiary stereocenters. Among four possible stereoisomers, one stereoisomer can be selectively produced in high yield, enhancing the feasibility of the T-T strategy, particularly in the synthesis of spirocarbocycles.</AbstractText>
